# ETheory's Spell-On Qualitative Inquiry and Educational Research.

**Authors:** Thomas, Gary

## Abstract
Challenges theory's secure place in qualitative inquiry on three counts. Argues (1) the search for theory in such inquiry originates in a crypto-functionalism; (2) theory's supposed importance for policy formulation cannot in itself justify it; and (3) arguments about its successful use are belied by examining discussion about theory in those arenas. (BT)

**Source:** https://eric.ed.gov/?id=EJ678394

